OL,3,GNEWSAPlanning decision success
OL,4,Aimproving, says council
OL,5,
OL,6,FA local authority has said it is moving
OL,7,Fin the right direction after it was
OL,8,Fstripped of its ability to make
OL,9,Fdecisions on major planning
OL,10,Fapplications.
OL,12,FIn June, Cherwell District Council was
OL,13,Fdesignated - allowing developers to
OL,14,Fbypass the council and submit their
OL,15,Fplans straight to the Planning
OL,16,FInspectorate.
OL,18,FAt the time, the Liberal Democrat
OL,19,Fleader of the authority, Lesley McLean,
OL,20,Fsaid the government's decision was
OL,21,F"disappointing and, frankly,
OL,22,Ffrustrating".
OL,23,APub: 18-OctQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
